.TH V23-FORTUNED 8
.SH NAME
v23/fortuned \- Vanadium RPC fortune server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B v23/fortuned
[
.B -a
.I addr
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I V23/fortuned
creates a server principal, announces on
.I addr
(default
.BR tcp!*!3245 ),
and serves a tiny fortune service over
.IR v23-rpc (2).
.PP
Methods:
.TP
.B Get
Returns a fortune string (empty arg).
.TP
.B Add
Appends
.I arg
to the in-memory fortune list.
.PP
Incoming clients are authorized with ACL
.BR ...
(TOFU: first peer blessings are trusted as roots).
.PP
.B /net
must be in the name space.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/v23/fortuned.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR v23-fortune (1),
.IR v23-rpc (2),
.IR v23-intro (2),
.IR dial (2)
.SH BUGS
.IP \(bu
Fortunes are not persisted.
.IP \(bu
ACL
.B ...
accepts any first presenter; not suitable for hostile networks.
.IP \(bu
No graceful shutdown beyond process exit; hung clients can block accept
depending on
.IR v23-rpc (2)
implementation.
.IP \(bu
Networked smoke tests against this server have not been fully verified
when
.B /net
was unavailable.
.SH TODO
.IP \(bu
